// `min / -1` is the one division that overflows, and the one the hardware traps on.
//
// The VM has to catch it before the divide instruction runs: on x86 a 32 bit `idiv` with
// this input raises #DE, which is not a signal the interpreter can turn into a language
// trap. The generic path checks the pair explicitly, and so does the fast path, but only a
// test proves both do.
//
// The companion file mod_int32_min.ax checks the other half of the same coin: the same
// operands under `%`, where the answer is 0 and nothing should trap.

function main():void {
    print("before\n");
    int32 lowest = -2147483647 - 1;
    int32 minusOne = 0 - 1;
    int32 boom = lowest / minusOne;
    print(boom);
    eof: pass;
}
